                     domains are found at the C-terminus of secreted proteins
                     in organisms that possess both rhombosortase, which is an
                     intramembrane serine proteinase (see TIGR03902), and a
                     type II secretion system (T2SS). In at least some cases,
                     such as VesB from Vibrio cholerae, cleavage by
                     rhombosortase is followed first by attachment of a
                     glycerophosphoethanolamine-containing moiety, then by
                     transport by the T2SS across the outer membrane and
                     release into the medium in soluble form; Derived by
                     automated computational analysis using gene prediction
                     method: Protein Homology."
